      "writtenOn": "2017-06-12T14:59:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I found the goto a bit confusing. Since most of the function is actually covered between the goto and the goto label, why not just call the function twice?\nThat way its purpose is quite clear: computing the group energy. Hence I would propose to call sched_group_energy().\nYou would move the tiny bit of bookkeeping (summing up the energy results, and setting/restoring util_delta) to the parent function, but in terms of LOC it shouldn\u0027t be a massive change.\nSince the parent function is already called sched_group_energy() I would propose to call it h_sched_group_energy() as it is basically just traversing the sched_domain hierarchy to compute the hierarchical energy.",
      "parentUuid": "251b608c_7e76ca92",
