      "writtenOn": "2017-06-13T11:46:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t like the \"h_sched_group_energy()\" name... what about just \"_sched_group_energy()\"?\n\nOr otherwise, since the parent call now is computing both the before and the after energies, we should rename that function and use sched_group_energy for the inner-most.\n\nWhat about something like\n\n energy_diff(eenv) // compute the energy diff\n   -\u003e compute_energy(eenv) // compute the energy for different confs (i.e. with and without util_delta)\n      -\u003e sched_group_energy(eenv) // compute the energy for one conf\n\nBut for the rest, as I was proposing to Brenda, I can try to have most of the code in an inline function while moving the bookkeeping the parent as you propose.",
      "parentUuid": "849827f9_4dd8ba4f",
      "revId": "7e70501ce9797381262073463e9fa7f42978ce29",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
