    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5a71dd8_81aac246",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/fair.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 5446,
      "author": {
        "id": 1119068
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-29T09:20:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just noticed that s/sched_group_energy/compute_energy/ allows also to solve the ambiguity of \"sched_group_energy\", which is a name currently used both for a function and a struct.\n\nRegarding the inlining instead, despite it can simplify the current code, it is also not suitable for a clean integration of the following patches. Indeed, SchedTune needs to compute performance variations as well as energy variations. The current code structure, where we call a before_after_energy, allows to easily plug in the computation of these additional metrics into the existing code.\n\nThe same would not be as straightforward if we do the updates suggested by Morten. Thus for the time being I would still prefer to keep the single call we have now.",
      "parentUuid": "bb10c4b2_a8c5cc11",
      "revId": "7e70501ce9797381262073463e9fa7f42978ce29",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
