    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0e26a215_4fbcda45",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/fair.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 5493,
      "author": {
        "id": 1119068
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-12T12:55:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Referring to @brendan \"I don\u0027t understand the check for the group_weight of sg_shared_cap\", here it works that way:\n\n- line 5481: if we are at MC level (one single CPU), then we keep track of the above SD in sg_shared_cap, since this defines the set of CPUs which shares their capacity\n\nNOTE: here we have already many hardcoded assumption, like we have only MC and DIE level and the frequency domains match the SGs at DIE level.\nNOTE2: goal of this patch is NOT to make the code more generic, but just more easy to understand and more efficient at run-time. Further optimizations IMO should be done in a second step.\n\n- line 5484: visit SD bottom-up, from MC (each CPU) to DIE (each cluster)\n\n- line 5488: that\u0027s a bottom-up visit required check, since we scan all the CPUs (line 4751) we will end up visiting the DIE SG for each CPU in a cluster multiple times... this check enfore the evaluation of the cluster energy just one time.\n\nNOTE: the top-down approach I proposed in the past does not have this \"issue\" but there was potentially other problems.\n\nFinally:\n\n- line 5493: if this SG\u0027s does not contain the same number of CPUs of the sg_shared_cap we cached at line 5481, than this means we are at looking at a CPU at MC level. Thus, we need to update the sg_cap pointer to reference the topmost SG (DIE level) which will be used to compute the SG\u0027s capacity from one of the following functions:\n\n   sched_group_energy()\n      -\u003ebefore_after_energy()\n         -\u003efind_new_capacity()\n            -\u003egroup_max_util()\n\nwhich ultimately computes the maximum utilization of all the CPUs in the shared capacity domain. This value is what defines the OPP to consider for the energy contribution of the current CPU.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5493,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 5493,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "7e70501ce9797381262073463e9fa7f42978ce29",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
